    "updated_at": "2016-08-26T17:18:26Z",
    "body": "> Yeah, that's in the commit queue as we speak: https://codereview.chromium.org/2278823004/\n\n<3!\n\n> The fallback values are valuable, I think, but could an author include multiple meta referrer elements to get that behavior? That is, maybe each meta referrer need only contain a single token, and you can have multiple meta referrer elements to get the fallback behavior?\n\nGood point! Yeah, the later ones in the document will override the earlier ones, if they contain valid referrer policies.\n\nShould we specific that Firefox behavior of only matching a single token, and are you willing to implement it in Chrome? It would be backward-incompatible, because things like `no-referrer-when-downgrade,unsafe-url` would be just ignored instead of picking the last one :-/.\n",
